stitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to (4,4)}\\frac{x-y}{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y}}=\\frac{4-4}{\\sqrt{4}-\\sqrt{4}}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by first multiplying the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (4,4)}\\frac{x-y}{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y}} & =\\lim_{x\\to (4,4)}\\frac{(x-y)(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})}{(\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y})(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (4,4)}\\frac{(x-y)(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})}{(\\sqrt{x})^{2}-(\\sqrt{y})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (4,4)}\\frac{(x-y)(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})}{x-y} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (4,4)}(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (4,4)}(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y}) & =\\sqrt{4}+\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2+2 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $4.$"}] [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc9b3e9b-4cb6-5677-b761-23778c11ba6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(y^{2} - 2x)e^{xy} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186144310} {:answer/id #uuid "eac5ffb8-9406-5c23-933c-5caad9ecf4d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y^{2} + e^{xy} + 2x - 2 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186144311} {:answer/id #uuid "f51f2ba6-8bad-5c55-b62a-2166e90facb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y^{2} - e^{xy} - 2x = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186144312} {:answer/id #uuid "fb535711-80ea-563e-b11b-27400ae5d2ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{xy} - y^{2} + 2x = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186144313} {:answer/id #uuid "2df2d011-4de8-5b39-a641-2ffb32198770" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y^{2} - e^{x + y} - 2x + (e - 1) = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186144314}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9950c51f-3179-5469-8fd1-4f7293c630f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1759